.TH TLS12TEST 1
.SH NAME
tls12test \- live end-to-end test of the TLS 1.2 client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tls12test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tls12test
exercises
.IR tls12 (2)'s
full client path \(em ClientHello through both Finished messages,
then real encrypted application data \(em against the two live hosts
.I doc/ssl-modernization-plan.md
measured its scope from, one per AEAD suite:
.IP 1.
.BR bsky.social :
both suites offered; the server picks
.B TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
(16rC02F), exercising the AES-GCM record path.
.IP 2.
.BR mastodon.social :
only
.B TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305
(16rCCA8) offered. Mastodon prefers GCM when both are on the table
(checked live, 2026-09-02), so narrowing the offer is what makes this
leg reach the ChaCha20-Poly1305 code at all.
.PP
Each leg sends a real HTTP/1.1 GET over the established session and
requires a decrypted response beginning
.B HTTP/1.
back.
.PP
Two in-test negative controls then attack the record layer of fresh
sessions, confirming the authentication is real rather than
decorative:
.IP 3.
the receive sequence number is corrupted before reading; the next
read must fail with a record-authentication error, since the AEAD's
additional data covers the sequence number. A read that still
succeeds means the tag check is not actually tied to the AAD, and the
test fails.
.IP 4.
the send sequence number is corrupted before writing; the server must
refuse the request (an alert or a dead connection). A normal HTTP
response back means the server-side MAC check saw nothing wrong with
a desynchronized record, and the test fails.
.PP
Two further negative controls were run by hand against the library
when this test was built, per the repository's evidence discipline,
and are worth repeating after any change to the handshake: corrupting
one bit of the client Finished verify data made every server refuse
the handshake (mastodon with a fatal
.B decrypt_error
alert, description 51 \(em the exact alert RFC 5246 assigns to a bad
verify_data), and corrupting the expected server Finished value made
the client itself reject every handshake with a verify-data mismatch.
.PP
Both hosts are dialled by literal IP, compiled into the source \(em
.IR dialtest (1)
found
.I /net/cs
does not resolve names in this emu instance (a separate, tracked
gap); SNI needs only the hostname string.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/tls12test.b
