.SH BUGS
A pass proves a working, encrypted handshake and record layer against
today's server configuration \(em
.B not
an authenticated connection: certificate-chain verification does not
exist yet (see
.IR tls12 (2)'s
own BUGS). The test needs the real network, real third-party servers,
and their continued willingness to negotiate the measured suites;
none of that is under this tree's control, so a failure here can mean
the world changed rather than the code. The hand-run Finished
corruptions above are not automated, because they require corrupting
the library itself.
.SH HISTORY
.B Tls12test
supersedes
.BR tlshellotest (1),
the disposable step-4 probe that stopped after ServerHelloDone; the
probe's hand-rolled ClientHello encoding was absorbed into
.IR tls12 (2)
and the probe deleted, exactly as its own manual promised.
